@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title AJ Motors - Architecture
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #47665C
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #E5EDE4
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #F2ECD9
top to bottom direction

actor "Bruger" as customer
component "Frontend\nJava/Javalin + HTML/CSS/JS\nlocalhost:3000" as frontend
component "API Gateway\nlocalhost:8080" as gateway
component "Users\nlocalhost:7002" as users
component "Products (write)\nlocalhost:7003" as products
component "Orders\nlocalhost:7004" as orders
component "Payments (manual)\nlocalhost:7005" as payments
component "Product View (read)\nlocalhost:7006" as view
component "Product Synchronizer\nlocalhost:7007" as sync
component "Keycloak\nLocal third-party OIDC provider\nlocalhost:8180" as keycloak
database "Keycloak PostgreSQL\nPrivate identity store" as identityDb
queue "RabbitMQ\naj.events (topic exchange)\naj.users / aj.products / aj.orders / aj.payments / aj.product-sync\naj.dead (dead letters)" as rabbit
database "Users PostgreSQL\nlocalhost:5433" as usersDb
database "Products PostgreSQL\nlocalhost:5434" as productsDb
database "Orders PostgreSQL\nlocalhost:5435" as ordersDb
database "Payments PostgreSQL\nlocalhost:5436" as paymentsDb
database "Product View MongoDB\nPrivate product-view-data network\nproduct_view.products" as mongo

customer --> frontend : Browser
frontend --> gateway : HTTP /api/v1/*
frontend --> keycloak : OIDC Code + PKCE / SSO / logout
gateway --> keycloak : JWKS / discovery
keycloak --> identityDb : Own identity data
gateway --> users : HTTP users
gateway --> products : HTTP POST / PUT / DELETE products
gateway --> view : HTTP GET products
gateway --> orders : HTTP orders + user orders
gateway --> payments : HTTP payments + order payments
gateway --> sync : HTTP /health (status only)
users --> usersDb : JPA + outbox/inbox
products --> productsDb : JPA + outbox/inbox
orders --> ordersDb : JPA + outbox/inbox
payments --> paymentsDb : JPA + outbox/inbox
view --> mongo : Owned reads / versioned writes
sync --> view : Internal HTTP projection API + service token
users ..> rabbit : customer.valid / customer.invalid
rabbit ..> users : customer.check
orders ..> rabbit : customer.check / quantitycheck / order.cancelled\npayment.authorized / payment.rejected
rabbit ..> payments : payment.authorized / payment.rejected
rabbit ..> products : quantitycheck / order.cancelled\npaymentfail / payment.completed
products ..> rabbit : quantityreserved / quantityrejected\nproduct.created / updated / reserved / removed
rabbit ..> orders : customer.valid / invalid / quantityreserved / rejected\npayment.requested / paymentfail / payment.completed
payments ..> rabbit : payment.requested / payment.completed / paymentfail
rabbit ..> sync : product.*

note bottom of frontend
Frontend starts without backend dependencies.
Status polling and retry messages support partial outages.
Keycloak login is implemented; no Stripe.
Business role/ownership enforcement remains SEC-01.
end note
note bottom of mongo
Only Product View accesses the MongoDB read model.
Synchronizer relays events through the owner's API.
Each SQL service owns its own isolated database.
GUID references cross service boundaries; no cross-database FKs.
end note
legend bottom
Solid arrow: synchronous request / database access
Dashed arrow: asynchronous RabbitMQ delivery
service-common is a build library, not a running service.
endlegend
@enduml
